lesson: 100
title: Yards, feet and inches in two steps
stars: 2
explain: One yard is 3 feet, and one foot is 12 inches.
explain: When a story mixes units, turn everything into one unit, work out the story, then turn the answer into the unit the question asks for.
explain: A rope 4 yards long is 12 feet; cutting off 5 feet leaves 7 feet, and 7 feet are 7 × 12 = 84 inches.
vars: a=name b=name y=2..6 f=2..10 x=2..9
need: f < 3 * y
answer: (3 * y - f) * 12
exercise: A rope is {y} yards long. {a} cuts off {f} feet. How many inches of rope are left?
exercise: {a} buys {y} yards of ribbon and uses {f} feet of it for a bow. How many inches of ribbon are left?
exercise: A fence is {y} yards long. {f} feet of it are painted. How many inches are not painted yet?
exercise: {a} has a string {y} yards long and gives {f} feet of it to {b}. How many inches of string does {a} keep?
exercise: A hallway carpet is {y} yards long. {a} trims {f} feet from one end. How long is the carpet now, in inches?
exercise: A path is {y} yards long. {a} has walked {f} feet of it. How many inches are still to walk?
test: Of the {y} yards of cloth on a roll, a tailor sells {f} feet to {a}. How many inches of cloth stay on the roll?
test: {a} and {b} have a {y}-yard rope for their game. {b} cuts {f} feet off to tie {x} boxes. How many inches long is the rope they still have?
test: How many inches are left when {f} feet are cut from a hose {y} yards long?
test: {a} measures a board: {y} yards. {a.He} saws off a {f}-foot piece and cuts it into {x} small blocks. What length, in inches, is the rest of the board?
test: A garden bed {y} yards long has {f} feet planted with {x} rows of beans. How many inches of the bed have no beans yet?
exercise: {a} cuts {f} feet from a rope {y} yards long. How many inches of rope remain?
exercise: How many inches of ribbon are left if {f} feet are used from {y} yards of ribbon?
exercise: {y} yards of string, {f} feet cut off. How many inches are left?
exercise: A fence in Kansas is {y} yards long. {a} has painted {f} feet of it. How many inches still need paint?
exercise: {a} has {y.words} yards of cloth and sews {f.words} feet of it into a bag. How many inches of cloth are left?
exercise: A track in a school yard in Ohio is {y} yards long. {a} has run {f} feet of it. How many inches are still to run?
exercise: {a} buys a garden hose {y} yards long and cuts {f} feet off it for {b}. How many inches long is the hose {a} keeps?
exercise: A rug is {y} yards long. {f} feet of it are folded under the sofa. How many inches of rug can be seen?
test: In inches, how much of a {y}-yard rope is left after {a} takes {f} feet of it?
test: {b} lends {a} {f} feet from a {y}-yard roll of tape, and {a} uses the tape to wrap {x} gifts. How many inches of tape stay on the roll?
test: A hedge in Virginia runs {y} yards. A gardener trims {f} feet of it on Monday. How many inches of hedge are left to trim?
test: {a}'s kite string measures {y} yards. {f} feet tangle in a tree and are cut away. What length is left, in inches?
test: Of a {y}-yard bench, {f} feet are taken by {x} coats and bags. How many inches of the bench are free?
test: Subtract {f} feet from {y} yards. How many inches is the answer?
exercise: rope {y} yards, {a} chopped {f} feet off. inches left?
exercise: {a} bought {y} yards ribbon, used {f+1} — no wait, {f} feet. how many inches left
exercise: {b} says {(3*y-f)*10} inches cos 10 inches a foot. nah, {y} yd rope, {f} ft cut. inches left really
exercise: fence {y} yards, painted {f} feet so far, {a}'s {x} btw. how many inches not painted
test: {y} yd string, cut {f} ft, whats left in inches
test: {a} had {y+1} yards, sorry, {y} yards of tape, used {f} feet. inches remaining?
test: {a} reckons there's {3*y-f} inches left. nah that's feet innit. {y} yards, {f} feet gone. real inches?
exam: It is given that a rope measures {y} yards and that {f} feet are cut therefrom. Determine the remaining length, expressed in inches.
exam: Ascertain the length in inches of ribbon remaining after {a} has utilised {f.words} feet of a purchase of {y.words} yards.
exam: Whereas a strip of material of {y} yards is reduced by {f} feet, state the residual length in inches.
exam: Compute, in inches, the difference between a length of {y} yards and a length of {f} feet.
exercise: Grandad passed away and left {a} {y} yards of fishing line. {a} gives {f} feet of it to {b}. How many inches of line does {a} keep?
exercise: The "pre-loved" rope at the yard sale is {y} yards long, but {f} feet of it is frayed and cut off. How many inches of good rope are left?
test: {b}'s dog "left a present" on {f} ft of the {y}-yard rope, so that bit's binned. how many inches of rope are left, ugh
